<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  MARV SITL world.

  THE AIRCRAFT IS NOT INVENTED. The model below is the published "X3 UAV"
  (openrobotics/x3 uav, version 4) from Gazebo Fuel, copied verbatim -- mass
  1.5 kg, Ixx 0.0347563, Iyy 0.07, Izz 0.0977, rotor arms at (+/-0.13,
  +/-0.20..0.22) -- with exactly ONE addition: an IMU sensor on the base link.
  It descends from the RotorS simulator (Furrer et al., ETH Zurich), which is
  where those numbers were measured.

  The motor plugin parameters are the ones the shipped world
  /usr/share/gz/gz-sim8/worlds/multicopter_velocity_control.sdf uses for this
  same model: maxRotVelocity 800, motorConstant 8.54858e-06, momentConstant
  0.016, and the turningDirection assignment ccw/ccw/cw/cw on rotors 0..3.

  An earlier version of this file carried an airframe whose mass and inertias
  were made up. That was wrong on this project's own terms -- docs/validation.md
  requires constants to come from a primary source -- and it was not harmless:
  a symmetric invented inertia hid the fact that a real airframe has Ixx != Iyy,
  and an invented spin layout could not have caught the yaw sign error in
  core::presets::kQuadXPx4, which the published turningDirection assignment
  did catch.

  Thrust-to-weight here is about 1.47 (21.9 N against 14.9 N), so hover sits
  near 0.68 of command and a steep bank runs out of thrust. That is a property
  of the real aircraft, not of the harness, and the flight profile is sized to
  respect it.

  Physics at 1 kHz, real_time_factor 0: the harness steps this world
  (ADR-0002, lockstep) rather than watching it.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="marv">
    <physics name="1ms" type="dart">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-physics-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::Physics"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-user-commands-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-imu-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::Imu"/>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-air-pressure-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::AirPressure"/>
    <!-- Phase 5 unit 2a. The navsat system is what turns the <sensor
         type="navsat"> on the base link below into gz.msgs.NavSat traffic;
         without it the sensor element loads and publishes nothing, which
         looks exactly like a topic-name mistake. -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-navsat-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::NavSat"/>
    <!-- Magnetometer system, phase 5 unit 5a (ADR-0007 D35). Both params are
         set EXPLICITLY; at -v 4 the plugin prints what it used
         ("Magnetometer: using param [use_units_gauss: 0]", "[use_earth_frame_ned:
         0]"). false/false means: the message's field_tesla is in Tesla, and
         the world field the system computes from its tables (see the comment
         at <gravity> above -- it does NOT read a <magnetic_field> element) is
         expressed in ENU before the sensor rotates it into the body. The
         bridge's mag-vs-truth pin (unit 5a.1), not this comment, proves the
         frame and the unit. -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-magnetometer-system"
            name="gz::sim::systems::Magnetometer">
      <use_units_gauss>false</use_units_gauss>
      <use_earth_frame_ned>false</use_earth_frame_ned>
    </plugin>

    <gravity>0 0 -9.8066</gravity>
    <!-- No <magnetic_field> element, and that is deliberate (phase 5 unit
         5a.0, 2026-09-04): gz-sim 8's Magnetometer system recomputes the
         world field on every update from its own 10-degree tables at the
         <spherical_coordinates> below and overwrites whatever this element
         says (Magnetometer.cc:440-506, gz-sim8 branch) -- unit 5a.0 set it to
         WMM-2025 and read a different field off the topic. The field the
         sensor publishes is that table value, reproduced and probe-verified:
         NED (0.2162762, 0.0096861, 0.4291632) gauss, declination 2.5643 deg
         (docs/datasheets/wmm-zurich.md, second section; constants.hpp
         kGzMagFieldNedGauss). An element here would be a comment that lies;
         the harness's mag-vs-truth pin is what holds the value. -->

    <!-- WHERE THIS WORLD IS, and why it is not the equator.
         Phase 5 unit 2a (ADR-0007 S2): the navsat sensor reports latitude,
         longitude and altitude, and it can only do that against a stated
         origin. gz-sim's SphericalCoordinates turns the model's ENU world
         position into degrees about this datum, and sitl/src/gazebo_ports.cpp
         projects them back to NED metres -- so these five numbers and the
         GazeboConfig::gps_datum_* fields that mirror them are ONE fact
         written in two places, exactly as <update_rate>50</update_rate> on
         baro_sensor and GazeboConfig::baro_period_us already are.

         The place is ETH Zurich's Zentrum campus, 47.376388 N 8.547778 E,
         408 m -- the lab the X3 in this file was measured in (RotorS, Furrer
         et al., the provenance this file's own header records). A location
         has to be somewhere, and this aircraft's own is a better answer than
         a default.

         THE LATITUDE IS THE PART THAT MATTERS. The flat-earth projection
         scales east by cos(lat0) and north by the meridian radius; at
         latitude 0 the cosine is 1, the two radii are at their closest, and
         a projection that dropped the cosine, or crossed north with east,
         would read correct anyway. At 47.376388 deg cos(lat0) = 0.6773, so
         an east metre and a north metre differ by a third and neither
         mistake can hide. A datum on the equator would be a test that
         cannot fail.

         heading_deg 0, so the world frame is plain ENU (+X east, +Y north,
         +Z up) -- which is what the bridge's ENU->NED mapping assumes and
         what gz-sim documents its world frame to be. A nonzero heading
         would rotate the world's X/Y away from east/north and silently
         invalidate that mapping.

         The elevation only enters as a DIFFERENCE (down = -(alt - alt0)) and
         through the WGS-84 radii, where 408 m against 6.37e6 m is 6e-5 --
         it is stated rather than defaulted so the SDF's number and the
         bridge's can be compared by eye. -->
    <spherical_coordinates>
      <surface_model>EARTH_WGS84</surface_model>
      <world_frame_orientation>ENU</world_frame_orientation>
      <latitude_deg>47.376388</latitude_deg>
      <longitude_deg>8.547778</longitude_deg>
      <elevation>408</elevation>
      <heading_deg>0</heading_deg>
    </spherical_coordinates>

    <light type="directional" name="sun">
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 10 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.9 0.9 0.9 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>
    </light>

    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry><plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>200 200</size></plane></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>200 200</size></plane></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.3 0.32 0.3 1</ambient><diffuse>0.45 0.5 0.45 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="marv_quad">
    <!-- On the ground, at rest, which is where an aircraft powers up.
         0.055 m is half the base_link collision box height (0.11 m), so the
         box's underside sits exactly on the plane. The published X3 value,
         0.053302, started it 1.7 mm inside the ground. -->
    <pose>0 0 0.055 0 0 0</pose>

            <pose>0 0 0.055 0 0 0</pose>
            <link name="X3/base_link">
                <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                <inertial>
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <mass>1.5</mass>
                    <inertia>
                        <ixx>0.0347563</ixx>
                        <ixy>0</ixy>
                        <ixz>0</ixz>
                        <iyy>0.07</iyy>
                        <iyz>0</iyz>
                        <izz>0.0977</izz>
                    </inertia>
                </inertial>
                <collision name="X3/base_link_inertia_collision">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <box>
                            <size>0.47 0.47 0.11</size>
                        </box>
                    </geometry>
                </collision>
                <visual name="X3/base_link_inertia_visual">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <mesh>
                            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
                            <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/openrobotics/models/x3 uav/4/files/meshes/x3.dae</uri>
                        </mesh>
                    </geometry>
                </visual>
        
              <!-- The ONLY addition to the published X3 model. 1 kHz to match the
                   loop. Noise is the madflight FC3's LSM6DSV (docs/datasheets/LSM6DSV.pdf, DS13476 Rev 2):
                   per-sample sigma = noise density * sqrt(BW), BW = ODR/2 = 500 Hz (LPF1 cutoff in
                   high-performance mode, p.33 note 1; RMS noise is quoted at BW = ODR/2, p.11 note 9).
                   Turn-on bias per axis: zero mean, sigma = the typical zero-g / zero-rate level (the typical
                   level "describes the standard deviation" over parts, p.18 sec 4.6.2); gz flips its sign at random. -->
              <sensor name="imu_sensor" type="imu">
                <always_on>1</always_on>
                <update_rate>1000</update_rate>
                <imu>
                  <!-- Rn 2.8 mdps/sqrt(Hz) * sqrt(500 Hz) = 0.0626 dps = 1.093e-3 rad/s; G_TyOff 1 dps = 0.01745 rad/s (p.10 Table 2). -->
                  <angular_velocity>
                    <x><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>1.093e-3</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.01745</bias_stddev></noise></x>
                    <y><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>1.093e-3</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.01745</bias_stddev></noise></y>
                    <z><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>1.093e-3</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.01745</bias_stddev></noise></z>
                  </angular_velocity>
                  <!-- An 60 ug/sqrt(Hz) (HP) * sqrt(500 Hz) = 1.342 mg = 0.01316 m/s^2; LA_TyOff 12 mg = 0.1177 m/s^2 (p.10 Table 2). -->
                  <linear_acceleration>
                    <x><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.01316</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.1177</bias_stddev></noise></x>
                    <y><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.01316</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.1177</bias_stddev></noise></y>
                    <z><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.01316</stddev><bias_mean>0</bias_mean><bias_stddev>0.1177</bias_stddev></noise></z>
                  </linear_acceleration>
                </imu>
              </sensor>

              <!-- Barometer. 50 Hz, deliberately slower than the IMU's 1 kHz
                   so the multi-rate staleness machinery is actually exercised
                   rather than every sensor arriving in lockstep. -->
              <sensor name="baro_sensor" type="air_pressure">
                <always_on>1</always_on>
                <update_rate>50</update_rate>
                <!-- BMP580 (docs/datasheets/BMP580.pdf p.9 Table 1): Vp_hi_res 0.25 Pa RMS (max; typ 0.21). -->
                <air_pressure>
                  <pressure><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.25</stddev></noise></pressure>
                </air_pressure>
              </sensor>

              <!-- GPS, phase 5 unit 2a. 10 Hz, the NEO-M9N's own rate and the
                   one MultiRateSource has always synthesised
                   (sitl/include/marv/sitl/sources.hpp) -- a hundred control
                   frames per sample, so the staleness the frame contract
                   describes is real rather than nominal.

                   Noise: the FC3's GPS is an external module the board does not
                   specify, so the values below are an ASSUMPTION of a u-blox
                   M10-class receiver: position sigma 1.0 m horizontal, 1.5 m
                   vertical, velocity sigma 0.05 m/s, white at 10 Hz.

                   The topic is gz-sim's own default for a navsat sensor --
                   scopedName + "/navsat", VERIFIED against the running world
                   with `gz topic -l` rather than assumed -- and
                   marv::sitl::gps_topic() (sitl/src/gazebo_ports.cpp) must
                   read identically to this sensor's NAME, exactly as
                   imu_topic and baro_topic do for theirs. -->
              <sensor name="gps_sensor" type="navsat">
                <always_on>1</always_on>
                <update_rate>10</update_rate>
                <navsat>
                  <!-- ASSUMED u-blox M10 class. gz-sensors 8 applies the horizontal noise to latitude and longitude in
                       DEGREES (NavSatSensor.cc, Update): 9.0e-6 deg = 1.0 m north, 0.68 m east at 47.38 deg N. -->
                  <position_sensing>
                    <horizontal><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>9.0e-6</stddev></noise></horizontal>
                    <vertical><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>1.5</stddev></noise></vertical>
                  </position_sensing>
                  <velocity_sensing>
                    <horizontal><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.05</stddev></noise></horizontal>
                    <vertical><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>0.05</stddev></noise></vertical>
                  </velocity_sensing>
                </navsat>
              </sensor>

              <!-- Magnetometer, phase 5 unit 5a. 100 Hz, PROVISIONAL: a
                   BMM350 output-data-rate the phase 7 driver will pick from
                   the datasheet (not yet in docs/datasheets/), fast enough
                   that the yaw datum lands before the first GPS fix at
                   0.199 s and slow enough to stay a multi-rate sensor rather
                   than a second IMU. Its period (10 ms) is under the baro's
                   (20 ms), so prime()'s step floor, max(2 baro, 2 GPS
                   periods), does not move and frame 0 stays at 201 000 us.

                   Noise: the FC3's MMC5603NJ, below.

                   The topic is gz-sim's default, scopedName + "/magnetometer"
                   (the literal in libgz-sim8-magnetometer-system.so), and
                   marv::sitl::mag_topic() (unit 5a.1) must read identically
                   to this sensor's NAME, as imu_topic, baro_topic and
                   gps_topic do for theirs. Nothing subscribes to it in unit
                   5a.0; the nine graded profiles must not move. -->
              <sensor name="mag_sensor" type="magnetometer">
                <always_on>1</always_on>
                <update_rate>100</update_rate>
                <!-- MMC5603NJ (docs/datasheets/MMC5603NJ.pdf p.2): total RMS noise 2.0 mG = 2.0e-7 T per axis at BW=01,
                     the bandwidth whose max ODR (150 Hz) covers 100 Hz. The field here is in tesla (use_units_gauss 0). -->
                <magnetometer>
                  <x><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>2.0e-7</stddev></noise></x>
                  <y><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>2.0e-7</stddev></noise></y>
                  <z><noise type="gaussian"><mean>0</mean><stddev>2.0e-7</stddev></noise></z>
                </magnetometer>
              </sensor>
            </link>
            <link name="X3/rotor_0">
                <pose>0.13 -0.22 0.023 0 -0 0</pose>
                <inertial>
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <mass>0.005</mass>
                    <inertia>
                        <ixx>9.75e-07</ixx>
                        <ixy>0</ixy>
                        <ixz>0</ixz>
                        <iyy>4.17041e-05</iyy>
                        <iyz>0</iyz>
                        <izz>4.26041e-05</izz>
                    </inertia>
                </inertial>
                <collision name="X3/rotor_0_collision">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <cylinder>
                            <length>0.005</length>
                            <radius>0.1</radius>
                        </cylinder>
                    </geometry>
                    <surface>
                        <contact>
                            <ode/>
                        </contact>
                        <friction>
                            <ode/>
                        </friction>
                    </surface>
                </collision>
                <visual name="X3/rotor_0_visual">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <mesh>
                            <scale>0.1 0.1 0.1</scale>
                            <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/openrobotics/models/x3 uav/4/files/meshes/propeller_ccw.dae</uri>
                        </mesh>
                    </geometry>
                    <material>
                        <script>
                            <name>Gazebo/Blue</name>
                            <uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri>
                        </script>
                    </material>
                </visual>
                <gravity>1</gravity>
                <velocity_decay/>
            </link>
            <joint name="X3/rotor_0_joint" type="revolute">
                <child>X3/rotor_0</child>
                <parent>X3/base_link</parent>
                <axis>
                    <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>
                    <limit>
                        <lower>-1e+16</lower>
                        <upper>1e+16</upper>
                    </limit>
                    <dynamics>
                        <spring_reference>0</spring_reference>
                        <spring_stiffness>0</spring_stiffness>
                    </dynamics>
                </axis>
            </joint>
            <link name="X3/rotor_1">
                <pose>-0.13 0.2 0.023 0 -0 0</pose>
                <inertial>
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <mass>0.005</mass>
                    <inertia>
                        <ixx>9.75e-07</ixx>
                        <ixy>0</ixy>
                        <ixz>0</ixz>
                        <iyy>4.17041e-05</iyy>
                        <iyz>0</iyz>
                        <izz>4.26041e-05</izz>
                    </inertia>
                </inertial>
                <collision name="X3/rotor_1_collision">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <cylinder>
                            <length>0.005</length>
                            <radius>0.1</radius>
                        </cylinder>
                    </geometry>
                    <surface>
                        <contact>
                            <ode/>
                        </contact>
                        <friction>
                            <ode/>
                        </friction>
                    </surface>
                </collision>
                <visual name="X3/rotor_1_visual">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <mesh>
                            <scale>0.1 0.1 0.1</scale>
                            <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/openrobotics/models/x3 uav/4/files/meshes/propeller_ccw.dae</uri>
                        </mesh>
                    </geometry>
                    <material>
                        <script>
                            <name>Gazebo/Red</name>
                            <uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri>
                        </script>
                    </material>
                </visual>
                <gravity>1</gravity>
                <velocity_decay/>
            </link>
            <joint name="X3/rotor_1_joint" type="revolute">
                <child>X3/rotor_1</child>
                <parent>X3/base_link</parent>
                <axis>
                    <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>
                    <limit>
                        <lower>-1e+16</lower>
                        <upper>1e+16</upper>
                    </limit>
                    <dynamics>
                        <spring_reference>0</spring_reference>
                        <spring_stiffness>0</spring_stiffness>
                    </dynamics>
                </axis>
            </joint>
            <link name="X3/rotor_2">
                <pose>0.13 0.22 0.023 0 -0 0</pose>
                <inertial>
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <mass>0.005</mass>
                    <inertia>
                        <ixx>9.75e-07</ixx>
                        <ixy>0</ixy>
                        <ixz>0</ixz>
                        <iyy>4.17041e-05</iyy>
                        <iyz>0</iyz>
                        <izz>4.26041e-05</izz>
                    </inertia>
                </inertial>
                <collision name="X3/rotor_2_collision">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <cylinder>
                            <length>0.005</length>
                            <radius>0.1</radius>
                        </cylinder>
                    </geometry>
                    <surface>
                        <contact>
                            <ode/>
                        </contact>
                        <friction>
                            <ode/>
                        </friction>
                    </surface>
                </collision>
                <visual name="X3/rotor_2_visual">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <mesh>
                            <scale>0.1 0.1 0.1</scale>
                            <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/openrobotics/models/x3 uav/4/files/meshes/propeller_cw.dae</uri>
                        </mesh>
                    </geometry>
                    <material>
                        <script>
                            <name>Gazebo/Blue</name>
                            <uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri>
                        </script>
                    </material>
                </visual>
                <gravity>1</gravity>
                <velocity_decay/>
            </link>
            <joint name="X3/rotor_2_joint" type="revolute">
                <child>X3/rotor_2</child>
                <parent>X3/base_link</parent>
                <axis>
                    <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>
                    <limit>
                        <lower>-1e+16</lower>
                        <upper>1e+16</upper>
                    </limit>
                    <dynamics>
                        <spring_reference>0</spring_reference>
                        <spring_stiffness>0</spring_stiffness>
                    </dynamics>
                </axis>
            </joint>
            <link name="X3/rotor_3">
                <pose>-0.13 -0.2 0.023 0 -0 0</pose>
                <inertial>
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <mass>0.005</mass>
                    <inertia>
                        <ixx>9.75e-07</ixx>
                        <ixy>0</ixy>
                        <ixz>0</ixz>
                        <iyy>4.17041e-05</iyy>
                        <iyz>0</iyz>
                        <izz>4.26041e-05</izz>
                    </inertia>
                </inertial>
                <collision name="X3/rotor_3_collision">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <cylinder>
                            <length>0.005</length>
                            <radius>0.1</radius>
                        </cylinder>
                    </geometry>
                    <surface>
                        <contact>
                            <ode/>
                        </contact>
                        <friction>
                            <ode/>
                        </friction>
                    </surface>
                </collision>
                <visual name="X3/rotor_3_visual">
                    <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
                    <geometry>
                        <mesh>
                            <scale>0.1 0.1 0.1</scale>
                            <uri>https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/openrobotics/models/x3 uav/4/files/meshes/propeller_cw.dae</uri>
                        </mesh>
                    </geometry>
                    <material>
                        <script>
                            <name>Gazebo/Red</name>
                            <uri>file://media/materials/scripts/gazebo.material</uri>
                        </script>
                    </material>
                </visual>
                <gravity>1</gravity>
                <velocity_decay/>
            </link>
            <joint name="X3/rotor_3_joint" type="revolute">
                <child>X3/rotor_3</child>
                <parent>X3/base_link</parent>
                <axis>
                    <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>
                    <limit>
                        <lower>-1e+16</lower>
                        <upper>1e+16</upper>
                    </limit>
                    <dynamics>
                        <spring_reference>0</spring_reference>
                        <spring_stiffness>0</spring_stiffness>
                    </dynamics>
                </axis>
            </joint>
              <plugin filename="gz-sim-multicopter-motor-model-system"
                  name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
            <jointName>X3/rotor_0_joint</jointName>
            <linkName>X3/rotor_0</linkName>
            <turningDirection>ccw</turningDirection>
            <timeConstantUp>0.0125</timeConstantUp>
            <timeConstantDown>0.025</timeConstantDown>
            <maxRotVelocity>800.0</maxRotVelocity>
            <motorConstant>8.54858e-06</motorConstant>
            <momentConstant>0.016</momentConstant>
            <rotorDragCoefficient>8.06428e-05</rotorDragCoefficient>
            <rollingMomentCoefficient>1e-06</rollingMomentCoefficient>
            <rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>100</rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>
            <commandSubTopic>command/motor_speed</commandSubTopic>
            <actuator_number>0</actuator_number>
            <motorType>velocity</motorType>
          </plugin>
          <plugin filename="gz-sim-multicopter-motor-model-system"
                  name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
            <jointName>X3/rotor_1_joint</jointName>
            <linkName>X3/rotor_1</linkName>
